  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HYDROLOGICAL RESTORATION OF KEY WETLAND</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will: (1.a.) Restore the Hydrology of 10,000 meters of channels impacting (185.85..hectares/459.04 acres) of wetlands in the Alvarado Lagoon System. (1.b.) Within that same area,..restore (10 hectares/12.35 acres) through planting 10,000 native species of trees along riverbanks...(1.c.) Remove invasive weeds from (1 hectare/2.47 acres). (1.d.) Set up 10 perches and 25 artificial..shelters for fauna. (1.e.) Install 5,000 meters of fencing. These activities will take place on previously..protected areas. (1.f.) These areas are already legally protected, but the project will provide an..additional, 99-year layer of protection for 569 hectares/1,407.44 acres by obtaining ADVC certificates..from CONANP. (2) Monitor migratory bird abundance and richness. (3) Train 10 fishermen and..fisherwomen in community-based monitoring of fish and macroinvertebrates of ecological and..economic importance. (4) Raise awareness among 44 families of local fishing cooperatives to..improve their livelihoods and to encourage data-driven local decision-making</narrative>
  </description>
